# docs/508-azure-managed-identity-docs).

ghpull:557 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "docs: surface Tier 3 Azure Managed Identity auth in README and deployment guide" ;
    bl:number 557 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:508 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr557 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:508 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-18T18:09:54Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr557Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #508 flagged that PR #506 (issue #58) documented Tier 3 Azure Managed Identity auth thoroughly in docs/plans/AUTH.md, but only there — README.md's Authentication table and docs/user/deployment.md's Authentication section, the two user-facing places Tiers 0-2 live, stopped at Tier 2, so a reader following the documented README -> deployment.md path would never discover Tier 3 existed. Reading AUTH.md's Tier 3 section (both the incoming and outgoing Managed Identity directions, the two Entra ID setup gotchas, and pr-506.ttl's own provenance summary) before writing anything confirmed the actual shipped scope: the incoming direction reuses Tier 2's OidcConfig::azure() validation unmodified (verified against sparql_endpoint/src/lib.rs and the entra_managed_identity.rs tests), while the outgoing direction (dagalog reading/writing Azure Blob Storage via its own Managed Identity) was deliberately deferred to a separate follow-up issue rather than implemented. The distillation into deployment.md therefore states the outgoing direction as 'not yet implemented' with a link back to AUTH.md's design sketch, rather than presenting pseudocode as a working feature — the key judgment call versus a straight copy of the planning doc. CLI flag names (--oidc-issuer, --oidc-audience, etc.) and OidcConfig::azure()'s issuer-format doc comment were cross-checked against src/main.rs and sparql_endpoint/src/lib.rs directly rather than trusted from AUTH.md, since planning docs can drift from shipped code. quickstart.md was left untouched per the issue's explicit out-of-scope note. The only quality-gate friction was environmental: cargo test --workspace initially failed with 'No space left on device' from the shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR filling up from concurrent worktree builds (a known hazard documented in CLAUDE.md), resolved with cargo clean once no other worktree was mid-build; the one remaining failure (query_timeout's 3,000,000-node OOM-SIGKILL test) is a documented pre-existing memory constraint of this 3.7GB sandbox, unrelated to a docs-only diff, and reproduces identically in isolation." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:557 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr557 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

